# MDLBeast Member App — Project Context for Cursor AI

This is the **MDLBeast Member App** — a React Native (Expo) mobile application
for members of MDLBeast's private club. Jira project: **MAR** (board 490),
61 tickets across 15 epics.

## Tech Stack
- **Framework**: React Native with Expo SDK 56+ (managed workflow)
- **Language**: TypeScript — strict mode. NEVER use `any`.
- **Navigation**: Expo Router (file-based, app/ directory)
- **Styling**: NativeWind v4 (Tailwind CSS utility classes). Do NOT use `StyleSheet.create`.
- **Server State**: TanStack Query v5
- **Global State**: Zustand
- **HTTP**: Axios with interceptors for PeopleVine token refresh (MAR-23)
- **Secure Storage**: Expo SecureStore (auth tokens, passcode hash)
- **Biometrics**: Expo Local Authentication (FaceID/fingerprint — MAR-20, MAR-21)
- **WebView**: react-native-webview (booking flows: SevenRooms, SynXis, Webstore)
- **Images**: Expo Image (with Cloudinary CDN + blurhash placeholders)
- **CMS**: Strapi v5 (all editorial content — amenities, FAQs, T&Cs, Privé/Attaché)

## Membership Tier System (CRITICAL)
Every member has a tier returned from PeopleVine at login. Tier drives navigation,
homepage variant, and feature visibility throughout the app.

```
type Tier = 'visitor' | 'pool_club' | 'prive' | 'unstable';
```

- **visitor**     — Browse only, no bookings. Sees Visitor Homepage (MAR-24)
- **pool_club**   — Pool, Gym, Restaurant, Rooms, Shisha bookings. (MAR-25)
- **prive**       — Pool Club + Privé benefits/rules/what's-on. (MAR-26)
- **unstable**    — All above + Attaché concierge + exclusive events. (MAR-27)

Tier routing (MAR-28) runs immediately after login. Use `<TierGate minimum="prive">`
to wrap tier-restricted content.

## Third-Party Booking Integrations (all WebView-based)
- **SevenRooms** → Restaurant table bookings (MAR-39, MAR-40)
- **SynXis** → Hotel room / stay bookings (MAR-43, MAR-44, MAR-45)
- **Webstore (MDLBeast)** → Gym PT sessions (MAR-36), Shisha (MAR-47)

Tickets marked `[Webstore]` are WebView-driven. Use the shared `WebViewScreen` component;
pre-fill member params; listen for return deep-link to confirm/cancel.

## Coding Conventions
- Always handle loading, error, and empty states.
- Tier-restricted screens MUST be wrapped in `<TierGate>`.
- All API calls go through services/ (peoplevine.ts, strapi.ts, sevenrooms.ts, synxis.ts).
- Auth tokens go through Expo SecureStore — never AsyncStorage.
- Path alias: `@/*` resolves to project root.
- File names: kebab-case for route files (e.g. `pool-club.tsx`),
  PascalCase for components (e.g. `BookingCard.tsx`).
- Reference Jira ticket in feature commits: `feat(MAR-XX): description`.

## Build Phases (reference)
1. Foundation & Auth (MAR-4, 5, 16-23, 60)
2. Homepage & Tier Routing (MAR-24-28)
3. Native Amenity Screens (Pool, Gym, Restaurant LP, Shisha LP)
4. WebView Booking Flows (MAR-36, 39, 43, 44, 45, 47)
5. Privé, Attaché, Support (MAR-48-53, 57-59)
6. Settings & Polish (MAR-54, 61, 62, 65 + EAS Build + Sentry)
